title: Hard Line Breaks Plugin
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<<.from-version "5.5.0">> The Hard Line Breaks plugin adds a hard line break syntax to WikiText: two spaces, or two spaces and a backslash, before the line end make a break anywhere, list items and headings included, as in [[CommonMark|https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#hard-line-breaks]]. A blank line still separates paragraphs.

See [ext[https://tiddlywiki.com/plugins/tiddlywiki/hard-line-breaks|plugins/tiddlywiki/hard-line-breaks]]

<<wikitext-example-without-html src:"""* Roses are red
Violets are blue
* Sugar is sweet  \
And so are you""">>

`\rules except ssnl` switches the rule off. The backslash form survives editors that trim trailing whitespace, so an editor that writes WikiText should prefer it.
